**Request \[[Create API Key](https://ultracart.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ucdoc/pages/38688545/API+Simple+Key)\]**
```bash
# getOrdersByRma: GET /order/orders/rma/{rma} (scope: order_read)
# Returns the orders with an exact RMA match. Wildcards such as * are rejected with a 400.
# Optional: _limit (max 1000), _offset, _sort, _expand.
# This lookup is backed by the search index, so a just-assigned RMA may take a short time to appear.
curl -X GET "https://secure.ultracart.com/rest/v2/order/orders/rma/RMA-12345\\ \
?_limit=100&_offset=0&_expand=summary" \
  -H "Accept: application/json" \
  -H "X-UltraCart-Api-Version: 2017-03-01" \
  -H "x-ultracart-simple-key: 55f7c4940f843d01a10c5d77f17001009dcc02345e79bd01a10c5d77f1700100"
```

**Response Body**
```json
{
    "orders": [
        {
            "merchant_id": "DEMO",
            "order_id": "DEMO-0009104390",
            "current_stage": "Shipping Department",
            "creation_dts": "2020-09-25T11:48:56-04:00",
            "language_iso_code": "ENG"
        }
    ],
    "success": true,
    "metadata": {
        "payload_name": "orders"
    }
}
```
